cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this in your research or tooling, please cite it as below."
title: "MRFoundry: AI for MRI research"
abstract: >-
  MRFoundry is an open-source skill package for AI-assisted magnetic resonance
  imaging (MRI) research. It connects domain knowledge, established scientific
  tools, experiment checks and project memory across physics, acquisition,
  reconstruction, analysis and scientific writing. Researchers set the goals
  and review the evidence; agents use composable instructions, references and
  helper scripts to plan, execute and revise the work. Scoped project lessons
  can guide subsequent tasks, while generalizable improvements enter shared
  skills through reviewed contributions. This researcher-guided
  self-improvement workflow updates reusable knowledge and procedures rather
  than model weights. The skill collection can grow as researchers contribute
  new methods, tools and checked workflows.
